From: Shahtyor <pepsykolya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:45:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] FreeForgeMiner 1.2.3: pipelined pool session (GPU never
 waits for the pool)

The GPU searches batch after batch on its own thread; the session thread sends every share of
a finished batch without waiting for the verdict (PoolClient::send_share), reads verdicts and
jobs as they arrive, resends verifier_busy/worker_busy/share_rate_limited shares after 250 ms
and hands the GPU the newest job. The searcher reports all shares of a batch and continues
after it (search_batch): upstream stopped at the first share and recomputed the rest.
The hashrate is wall-clock between batch completions (pool waits count against it).
Kavatar pool: GPU idle 13-20 % -> 0 %; RTX 4070 Ti 35.08 FW/s @179 W, RTX 3070 eco 19.93 @156 W.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
